pin start
name: pin-top
top
paragraph start
name: paragraph-this-pin-shows
This pin shows in reading mode and in writing mode. Its first
line is top, with no mode word, so it is for both modes. Pins
for both modes always sit first, above the mode pins. Why: this
is the one note every reader and every writer needs. Any block
can be pinned, and a pinned block also stays in the page body.
contract start
id: q94fc72
question: Does the paragraph make one point?
contract end
answer start
for: q94fc72
asked: Does the paragraph make one point?

answer end
paragraph end
pin end
pin start
name: pin-top-write
top write
paragraph start
name: paragraph-this-pin-shows-2
This pin shows only in writing mode. Its first line is top
write. Why: while you write you need the pin syntax at hand,
which is pin start, then top or bottom, then write or read for
one mode only, then pin end. A reader does not need it, so it
is gone in reading mode.
contract start
id: q94fc72
question: Does the paragraph make one point?
contract end
answer start
for: q94fc72
asked: Does the paragraph make one point?

answer end
paragraph end
pin end
pin start
name: pin-bottom-read
bottom read
paragraph start
name: paragraph-this-pin-shows-3
This pin shows only in reading mode, at the bottom. Its first
line is bottom read. Why: a reader may see a pinned block twice,
once pinned and once in the page body. That is on purpose, the
pin keeps it in sight while the page scrolls. A writer does not
need this note, so it is gone in writing mode.
