paragraph start
name: paragraph-the-pin-block
The pin block keeps what it holds on screen. Write pin start,
then top or bottom on the first line, then write or read if the
pin is for one mode only. With no second word it shows in both
modes. Then any blocks or whole chapters, then pin end. The
editor draws it when the file opens, with no command and no
scrolling. Pins for both modes sit first, mode pins under them.
Why: a rule, a formula or a chapter you keep needing stays in
sight on a small screen.
contract start
