code start
name: code-notation-render-file
language: text
notation render FILE  |  plain text render
notation render-rich FILE  |  unicode render
notation roundtrip FILE  |  prove the print back is identical
notation todos FILE  |  list every todo with its line
notation edition FILE  |  pages; flags --width W --lines L
notation index FOLDER  |  build .notation/index.db for the folder
ecosystem-server load FOLDER  |  server indexes and keeps the index
ecosystem-server links FILE  |  links written in a file of the index
ecosystem-server backlinks NAME  |  links that point to a block name
ecosystem-server broken  |  links whose target does not exist
ecosystem-server names  |  every block name with its file
ecosystem-server reload  |  reindex the folder of the last load
notation links FILE  |  load reload links backlinks broken names: the CLI sends them to the server, no server exits 1
notation new FILE  |  page text on stdin, the server writes it and commits
notation contracts FILE  |  and fill write through the server too, no server: direct write
ecosystem-server git FILE  |  repo, git name and email, clean or dirty
AIU_SERVER_PORT  |  HTTP port on 127.0.0.1, default 8080
AIU_WEBSITE_DIR  |  folder the HTTP door serves, default website
ws://127.0.0.1:PORT  |  WebSocket door, one command per text message
changed  |  text pushed to every WebSocket client after a reindex
ecosystem live aiu-notation-wasm  |  build notation.wasm for the browser
ecosystem live aiu-website  |  build bridge.wasm, the website wasm
bridge command(ptr,len)  |  wasm export, sends one command to the server
bridge answer_ptr, answer_len  |  wasm exports, the last answer text
ecosystem-server write PATH  |  text on the next lines, writes the file and commits
ecosystem-server delete PATH  |  saves in a commit, deletes, commits again
ecosystem-server move FROM  |  target on the next line, moves and commits
aiutd FILE  |  open in the editor, needs a real tty
aiutd update  |  compile, tests at a level, docs
aiutd test --level N  |  run tests; --only NAME for one
aiutd record NAME KEYS  |  record a test from a real run
aiutd record-module NAME PATH EXPR  |  record a module test
aiutd docs  |  write the tutorial from the notation files
