paragraph start
name: paragraph-links-a-target
Links: the link block is registered with its face and target
declarations. The box view draws the face, then the target in
parentheses: chapter number and title when the target is on the page, else its name. The index saves every link block, read from the parsed tree, with face, target, relation, mode and parent. The index run reports every link whose target is no block name and no file, and every name used twice, with their places and counts. Backlinks are computed from the link records, never stored. Mode live and copy write back: when a file is saved through the server, the body of the link block replaces the body of the target block in the source file of the target, and the server commits it. Why: one block is edited from every page that links to it. After a write the server reindexes the written file and every target file it changed, so links and backlinks show the edit at once, and it then pushes the message changed over WebSocket to every connected client. The editor part is not built yet.
contract start
id: q94fc72
