paragraph start
name: paragraph-master-view-map
Master view map. Layout files in notation/layouts say which files
appear in which box and where. Boxes nest, links draw as arrows,
and files in no layout wrap in a row. The page draws only files
under the scope key of the settings block, now demo/. Why: the demo must show
alone, and the maps live beside block types so deleting demo never
loses them. To see all files, set scope: all in layout-settings.aiu.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-master-view-look
Master view look. A settings block in notation/layouts holds the
card size, spacing, margin, header height and arrow curve. Why:
the look changes by editing notation, never code. Example: curve:
0.3 bends the arrows less than 0.5. Card text padding and font sizes are keys too: padv, padh, titlesize, descsize, labelsize. Colors and corners come only
from the theme.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-master-view-tap
Master view tap. Tap a card to light it and its linked cards,
tap it again to open the file, tap empty space to clear. Why: in
a big map you must see what a page connects to before opening it.
Phones send a fake mouse click after a touch, so mouse taps within
800 ms of a touch are ignored.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-master-view-demo
Master view demo. demo has 5 folders of 24 pages with random
links, and layout-demo-world nests the 5 folders. Why: to test
zoom, focus on tap and arrows on a map of about 125 pages.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-master-view-settings-tui
Settings TUI. Run settings-tui.rkt (in the ecosystem TUI configuration folder) from the AIU-ECOSYSTEM folder.
Up and down pick a setting, left and right change it, enter types
an exact value, q quits. Every change is saved to
layout-settings.aiu and the page reloads live. Why: the look must
be changed without touching code. Colors come from the theme.
paragraph end
